# PULL-UP

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Pull-Up is a bodyweight vertical pulling exercise designed to develop upper-body relative strength, grip strength and movement control.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the foundational exercises for assessing and developing upper-body pulling capacity.

---

# Philosophy

The Pull-Up represents one of the purest expressions of relative strength.

Unlike weighted variations, performance depends entirely on the athlete's ability to move their own body efficiently through space.

CAS frequently selects the Pull-Up for athletes requiring improved body control, pulling strength and strength-to-bodyweight ratio.

